{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1115425-castlevania-tv-series-is-ordo-dracul-revenge-story","id":1115425,"title":"Castlevania TV series is Ordo Dracul revenge story","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-13T01:17:03-07:00","id":1115425,"title":"Castlevania TV series is Ordo Dracul revenge story","content":"Netflix <b><i>Castelvania</i></b> anime series is really pumping me to run now Ordo Dracul vampires \u2013 shows picture Convent creator as omnipotent being, but fixated on understanding universe \u2013 and hating God and people following it. Certainly over powerful for <b>Requiem</b> take, sometimes, but it shows creation of Ordo Dracul philosophy rather good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yy_FWdbnvM0\" data-code=\"yy_FWdbnvM0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/yy_FWdbnvM0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T02:05:37-07:00","id":1115432,"title":"","content":"That show was really good IMO. Great voice actors and cool animation style. And some hilarious dialogue at the start of episode 2.<br /> <br /> Too bad it was only 4 episodes long, but apparently they are making a second season with 8 episodes. Season 2 is supposed to follow the story of Castelvania 3, with this season 1 being like the prequel to that story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T01:39:39-07:00","id":1117639,"title":"","content":"is it worth watching if you have no knowledge of the castelvania games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T02:09:36-07:00","id":1117645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ahather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1115425-castlevania-tv-series-is-ordo-dracul-revenge-story?p=1117639#post1117639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is it worth watching if you have no knowledge of the castelvania games?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't consider it a barrier, but you may find its appeal kind of limited. Both the anime (so far) and the specific game it's based on are pretty light in terms of plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>she/her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13652-manic-pixie-dreamcast","name":"Manic Pixie Dreamcast","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13652_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T03:06:43-07:00","id":1117656,"title":"","content":"I found anime very fun to watching - even if not knowIng anything about video games. If you like Ordo Dracul or monster hunters - you will love it! \ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T05:53:47-07:00","id":1117687,"title":"","content":"You know, its rather amusing, Castlevania's twist on the whole Dracula story. Now, in Castlevania, Dracula has a strong interest in pseudo-scientific things. You see lots of clockwork and victorian-esk kinda-steam-punk going on along side the magic. Meanwhile? The Belmonts and company always seem to rely entirely on magic or faith. The Belmont clan is renowned for their consecrated weapons. Several types of magicians have made their appearance throughout the series. The vampire hunters rely more on magic than science to defeat the forces of darkness. Meanwhile, in the actual book Dracula? Drac was all mysticism and darkness and secrets, while Van Helsing was the one using enlightenment and science to track down and defeat Dracula alongside magic. The positions are actually reversed from the Castlevania series.<br /> <br /> That's really a big part of Dracula legend these days, I suppose. Since the story used a mix of science and magic during it, even if it wasn't Drac's thing, even if it was meant to be <i>directly His opposite, </i>has still become a major part of the story. Dracula and victorian-era science bits have mixed together until they're now one.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't really call this an Ordo Dracul revenge story, though. Despite the sorta-steampunk in the Castlevania games, the main antagonist himself is actually closer to a Primordial Beast than anything else. The focus of the story is inevitably about the gathered monsters (kinship), the castle itself (the Lair), and a demon lord fulfilling his hunger for vengence and power while spreading nightmares among the people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-18-2017, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T12:23:13-07:00","id":1119052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1115425-castlevania-tv-series-is-ordo-dracul-revenge-story?p=1117687#post1117687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't really call this an Ordo Dracul revenge story, though. Despite the sorta-steampunk in the Castlevania games, the main antagonist himself is actually closer to a Primordial Beast than anything else. The focus of the story is inevitably about the gathered monsters (kinship), the castle itself (the Lair), and a demon lord fulfilling his hunger for vengence and power while spreading nightmares among the people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually really like this idea for VtR. Dracula was a Beast not a Vampire. His followers don't know that though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T15:07:09-08:00","id":1266795,"title":"","content":"Watching Season 2 of the series. Even if I still see Dracula as the Ordo Dracul progenitor we saw him in <b>VtR - </b>his War Council, on the other hand, seems to work like typical local structures of Invictus on the now war. They still are political backstabbers, even if they only preparing war plans to attack new town, for example. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Adding humans to War Council leads me to related question - <b>Can mortals have offices in Invictus by VtR standards?</b> Cause it'\u015b interesting portrayal in series...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T17:28:41-08:00","id":1266822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1115425-castlevania-tv-series-is-ordo-dracul-revenge-story?p=1266795#post1266795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watching Season 2 of the series. Even if I still see Dracula as the Ordo Dracul progenitor we saw him in <b>VtR - </b>his War Council, on the other hand, seems to work like typical local structures of Invictus on the now war. They still are political backstabbers, even if they only preparing war plans to attack new town, for example. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Adding humans to War Council leads me to related question - <b>Can mortals have offices in Invictus by VtR standards?</b> Cause it'\u015b interesting portrayal in series...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, ghouls and ghoul families could certainly have some sort of role as mouthpieces of certain elders and ancients, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T01:36:22-08:00","id":1266903,"title":"","content":"The more I see series, the clear is that <a href=\"http://castlevania.wikia.com/wiki/Speakers\" target=\"_blank\">Speakers</a> and <a href=\"http://castlevania.wikia.com/wiki/Devil_Forgemaster\" target=\"_blank\">Forgemasters</a> are mages, Obrimos and Moros respectively. Still humans, but having control over particular elements of the world.<br /> <br /> Series <a href=\"http://castlevania.wikia.com/wiki/Devil_Forgemaster\" target=\"_blank\">Wikia Forgemasters</a> page even more arguments for them being Moros:<br /> <i>' Devil Forgemasters are not mere sorcerers; they are not just trained in black magic, but also in the arts of alchemy and spiritual metaphysics, being able to craft massive weapons and arsenals from mere prime and raw materials of nearly any sort, as well as creating magical living beings with the forbidden knowledge they possess.'</i><br /> <br /> SO not only Death, but also Matter and Prime magic is at their disposal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T06:21:03-08:00","id":1266934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1115425-castlevania-tv-series-is-ordo-dracul-revenge-story?p=1119052#post1119052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually really like this idea for VtR. Dracula was a Beast not a Vampire. His followers don't know that though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really like the idea that Dracula in VtR has been deeply occulted and though he's pretty happy with the way the Ordo Dracul and Coils/Scales turned out, that wasn't his main point. <br /> <br /> He may not have even invented the coils--he just taught the foundations to his &quot;brides&quot; and let them advance the concepts. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T23:12:18-07:00","id":1375395,"title":"","content":"Returning to series on season 3...<br /> <br /> Do you know in what year Netflix series takes place? I try to sort out event in it in context of world's history...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Full timeline of the series, till season 3 - <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nRU-aR4buqU\" data-code=\"nRU-aR4buqU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/nRU-aR4buqU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-18-2020, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T00:34:59-07:00","id":1375556,"title":"","content":"In Season 3, <a href=\"https://castlevania.fandom.com/wiki/Council_of_Sisters\" target=\"_blank\">Council of Sisters</a> ruling Styria is looking like good model for Invictus Primogen Council in play. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[